SiteSentinel

This project is derived from "ppe-detection" by Cisco Systems, Inc.
(https://github.com/CiscoDevNet/ppe-detection), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. The detection model, the hard hat / vest matching idea,
and the backend /v1/detections contract originate there.

Modifications Copyright (c) 2026 Smit Mhatre. Changes from the original:
  - New web dashboard served by the backend (live compliance, incident log,
    photo evidence, hourly activity, camera status).
  - New video overlay replacing the TensorFlow Object Detection API drawing code.
  - Backend restructured into an in-memory event store plus JSON API; alerts
    reworded; Docker setup updated.
  - Detector refactored into run_detector.py, compliance.py and overlay.py.
  - Learned PPE association model (ml/) replaces the fixed overlap rule in the
    backend; camera simulator; Prometheus metrics.
  - DevOps pipeline: GitHub Actions and Jenkins CI/CD, Kubernetes manifests,
    deploy/rollback scripts, Prometheus alert rules and a Grafana dashboard.
